  "summary": "The email appears to be from a UK accommodation voucher service, stating a £450 voucher amount and providing a claim number (15541) for the recipient to use.",
  "explain": "The message contains no urgent threats, no request for credentials or personal data, no suspicious links or attachments, and its content is consistent with a simple voucher notification. Therefore it does not exhibit phishing indicators.",
  "is_phishing": "Clean"
}

{
  "summary": "The email is an automated error report displaying PHP warning and fatal error messages about a failed file include (permission denied) on a web server.",
  "is_phishing": "Clean",
  "explain": "The message contains only technical error information, lacks any request for credentials, urgent actions, links, attachments, or impersonation attempts, and therefore shows no phishing indicators."
}

{
  "summary": "The email, apparently from SendGreatOffers.com, advertises \"8 FREE Movie Tickets\" to the recipient JM@NETNOTEINC.COM and provides an unsubscribe link via admanmail.com.",
  "explain": "The message contains only a promotional offer and a standard unsubscribe link. It does not request credentials, personal data, or urgent action, and the link points to a legitimate email marketing domain. No malicious attachments or deceptive URLs are present, so it does not exhibit phishing characteristics.",
  "is_phishing": "Clean"
}

{
  "summary": "The email appears to be from an unknown sender and claims to redirect the recipient to a secure website, using a meta‑refresh tag that points to https://cktelefoonopstellenconfiguraties.nl/klanten/inloggen.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "code": "<meta content=\"0.0050; URL=https://cktelefoonopstellenconfiguraties.nl/klanten/inloggen\" http-equiv=refresh>",
      "code_explain": "A meta‑refresh automatically forwards the user to a non‑trusted domain (cktelefoonopstellenconfiguraties.nl). This is a classic phishing technique to lure victims to a fake login page for credential harvesting.",
      "tag": "SUSPICIOUS_LINK_CLICK"
    },
    {
      "code": "U wordt nu dooverwezen naar onze secure website...",
      "code_explain": "The message creates a sense of legitimacy and urgency by stating the user is being sent to a \"secure\" site, prompting the recipient to follow the redirect without questioning it.",
      "tag": "URGENCY_THREAT"
    },
    {
      "code": "https://cktelefoonopstellenconfiguraties.nl/klanten/inloggen",
      "code_explain": "The domain is a look‑alike/typosquatting URL that does not belong to any known brand, indicating a TYPOSQUATTING_DOMAIN used for credential harvesting.",
      "tag": "TYPOSQUATTING_DOMAIN"
    }
  ],
  "explain": "The email uses an automatic redirect to a suspicious, non‑brand domain and claims the destination is a secure login page, a typical credential‑harvesting phishing pattern.",
  "is_phishing": "Phishing",
  "tag": "CREDENTIAL_HARVESTING"
}

{
  "summary": "The email contains a dump of PHP warning messages from a website (zaborkursk.ru) and a JavaScript snippet that forces the browser to redirect to \"Login.php?sslchannel=true\".",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "code": "<script language=javascript>var page = \"Login.php?sslchannel=true\"; top.location = page;</script>",
      "code_explain": "The script automatically redirects the viewer to a login page, a classic technique for credential harvesting. It exploits the trust that the email appears to be a technical report, but the hidden redirect is a social‑engineering trigger to capture credentials.",
      "tag": "SUSPICIOUS_LINK_CLICK"
    },
    {
      "code": "Warning : fopen(assets/logs/ips.txt): failed to open stream: No such file or directory ...",
      "code_explain": "The inclusion of raw server error messages is unusual in legitimate business emails and serves to create a sense of urgency or technical issue, prompting the recipient to follow the hidden redirect. This is an HTML obfuscation/social‑engineering tactic.",
      "tag": "HTML_OBFUSCATION"
    }
  ],
  "explain": "The email embeds a JavaScript redirect to a login page without any visible link, aiming to harvest credentials. Combined with misleading PHP error output, this constitutes a phishing attempt.",
  "is_phishing": "Phishing",
  "tag": "SOCIAL_ENGINEERING"
}

{
  "summary": "The email pretends to be a WhatsApp payment verification page, asking the recipient to enter their Verified‑by‑Visa password, email address and email password to confirm a transaction.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "code": "Geben Sie Ihre Verified by Visa Passwort den Zahlungsvorgang zu bestätigen.",
      "code_explain": "Requests the victim’s Verified‑by‑Visa (3‑D Secure) password, a sensitive credential used for financial transactions. This is a classic credential‑harvesting prompt that leverages the urgency of confirming a payment.",
      "tag": "SENSITIVE_DATA_REQUEST"
    },
    {
      "code": "<form action=mpp2.php class=form-horizontal method=POST> ... <input class=inputsec name=3ds> ... <input class=forgoterinputer name=3dsemail> ... <input class=forgoterinputer name=3dsemailpass>",
      "code_explain": "HTML form that collects the 3DS password, the victim’s email address and the email password, then posts them to a suspicious script (mpp2.php). This is a direct credential‑harvesting mechanism.",
      "tag": "CREDENTIAL_HARVESTING"
    },
    {
      "code": "Diese Informationen werden nicht an den Händler übermittelt.",
      "code_explain": "False reassurance meant to lower the victim’s suspicion and encourage submission of credentials. Psychological trigger: trust through denial of data sharing.",
      "tag": "SOCIAL_ENGINEERING"
    },
    {
      "code": "<title> WhatsApp Secure </title> ... <h1>WhatsApp Messenger</h1> ... © 2016 WhatsApp Inc.",
      "code_explain": "Impersonates the WhatsApp brand (logo, copyright) to lend legitimacy to the phishing page – a brand impersonation tactic.",
      "tag": "BRAND_IMPERSONATION"
    },
    {
      "code": "<a href=http://blog.whatsapp.com/245/ target=_blank> Perché non vendiamo gli annunci </a>",
      "code_explain": "Provides a look‑alike WhatsApp blog URL to convince the user the page is official, while the surrounding page is malicious. This is a spoofed hyperlink / typosquatting indicator.",
      "tag": "TYPOSQUATTING_DOMAIN"
    }
  ],
  "explain": "The message contains multiple phishing indicators: it asks for Verified‑by‑Visa and email credentials, uses a fake payment‑verification form that posts to an unknown script, and impersonates WhatsApp to gain trust. These elements clearly aim to harvest financial and login credentials.",
  "is_phishing": "Phishing",
  "tag": "CREDENTIAL_HARVESTING"
}
